---
quiet: true
---
from_file env("TENZIR_INPUT") {
  read_json
}
this = {tetragon: this}
homelab::tetragon::ocsf::map tetragon, ocsf
this = move ocsf
ocsf_derive
ocsf_cast
// The direct leg's class gate, verbatim (nodes/tetragon/pipelines/
// tetragon-ocsf.tql): only the three archived classes reach the
// attest + to_clickhouse leg. The unmapped Base Event fallback
// (class_uid = 0 — the process_signal line) drops here and never
// reaches CH — the archive rule's types-scoping semantics carried
// in-stream, and the shape that keeps the to_clickhouse f-string's
// class_name non-null (the ocsf.null leak's kill, 27,987 rows
// pre-bump).
where class_uid in [ocsf_class_uid("Process Activity"), ocsf_class_uid("File System Activity"), ocsf_class_uid("Network Activity")]
// Pin the uids the direct leg mints with uuid() when absent: pinned
// fixtures keep the baseline deterministic (the investigations-test
// precedent). The arrival order below is deliberately ADVERSARIAL to
// the stamp order — this probe pins the windowed leg's ordering
// hypothesis (phase-2 launch brief, lap 2a-1):
//
//   arrival:  kprobe(05:05:34.89) file(05:06:05.00) exit(05:05:32.82)
//             exec(05:05:32.82) net(05:06:35.00) kprobe(05:05:59.00)
//             [unmapped signal]
//
// - exec and exit share ONE timestamp exactly (the same-second flood
//   burst shape): the (time, metadata.uid) sort must tie-break on uid
//   (exec < exit) even though exit ARRIVED first — the verify walk
//   re-sorts on the same pair, so a tie left to arrival order flags a
//   false chain_link_mismatch on the walk.
// - file and net arrive BETWEEN the W1 records (clock jumps to
//   05:06:05, then 05:06:35): exec/exit are out-of-order arrivals
//   (their window ends 05:06:00, within tolerance=30s of the clock)
//   and must still join W1 and stamp in time order.
// - the 05:06:35 arrival closes W1 (window end 05:06:00 + tolerance
//   30s): W1 stamps exec -> exit -> kprobe in one batch, W2 stamps
//   file -> net in the next — the cross-window seam this fixture can
//   pin is the chain-restart shape (a node context is not
//   fixture-testable, the tetragon-attest precedent: W2's first
//   record rides with no prev_event exactly like a fresh node's
//   first window); the LIVE seam (tetragon-chains context write ->
//   read landing across 60s-apart closures) carries the archive
//   rule's probed pass-to-pass semantics and is the lap-2a-2
//   server-side verification item.
if type_uid == 100701 {
  metadata.uid = "tet-direct-exec"
}
if type_uid == 100702 {
  metadata.uid = "tet-direct-exit"
}
if type_uid == 100700 and device.hostname == "talos-01" {
  metadata.uid = "tet-direct-kprobe"
}
if type_uid == 100700 and device.hostname == "talos-04" {
  metadata.uid = "tet-direct-late"
}
if type_uid == 100102 {
  metadata.uid = "tet-direct-file"
}
if type_uid == 400101 {
  metadata.uid = "tet-direct-net"
}
// The late kprobe (05:05:59, W1's range) arrives 36s behind the
// max observed clock (net, 05:06:35 — beyond tolerance=30s): in the
// LIVE stream the window operator drops such stragglers with a
// warning once their window has closed (reference/operators/
// window.md). A bounded fixture cannot reproduce that boundary —
// probed: window closures fire at input end on bounded reads (even
// with per-event batch separation), so the straggler joins W1 and
// the baseline must show it stamped in its CORRECT (time, uid) chain
// position (exec -> exit -> kprobe -> late-kprobe): the in-flight
// lateness the tolerance budget exists to absorb. The drop itself is
// live-stream behavior — the stated residual on the direct leg, and
// the lap-2a-2 server-side watch item.
// The direct leg's windowed attest shape, verbatim minus the node
// context lines (context_enrich / context_update — not fixture-
// testable, same omission as tetragon-attest) and the to_clickhouse
// sink (the baseline pins the stamped stream; the write leg is a
// sink and produces no output): the 60s event-time tumbling window
// bounds the sort (the archive rule sorted whole compaction passes;
// a sort on the unbounded flood stream is the walker's OOM class),
// and stream-mode attest chains the window's records in the sorted
// order via its internal lag. The per-window first record reads the
// pre-window chain tail in the live pipeline (the batch seam); here
// it rides the documented restart shape instead.
window size=60s, on=time, tolerance=30s, idle_timeout=120s {
  sort time, metadata.uid
  homelab::record_integrity::attest authority_uid="tenzir-node-tetragon",
    chain_uid="tenzir-node-tetragon",
    genesis=false,
    chain="stream"
}
